---
id: org.dxos.app.diagram
name: drawing.sh
version: 0.1.0
---

A diagramming app that is one full-screen canvas: open it and draw, with no sign-up. It is an app-framework
app with a small plugin set (the canvas, illustrator and space plugins plus its own layout plugin) rather than Composer
with things turned off. An identity is made silently on first run. Diagrams live in spaces, and a space is
shared with a link. The data and the link format are Composer's, so a space shared from Composer opens here and
one shared from here opens in Composer, with the same diagrams in both.

The app is drawing.sh ([D-144]). Each environment serves it at `app.` of its host, with the drawing.sh landing
site, its home page and its docs, at the host itself (F-13).

## Dependencies

```mdl
uses org.dxos.plugin.canvas: The scene editor every diagram opens in, its toolbar and palette, and the `Canvas` drawing variants.
```

```mdl
uses org.dxos.plugin.illustrator: The `Drawing` type a diagram is, its variants, and the create and convert operations.
```

```mdl
uses org.dxos.plugin.space: Composer's share link, root-collection filing, and its join, create-space and rename dialogs, which this app's layout shows.
```

```mdl
uses org.dxos.app.composer: The app a space shared from here must also open in.
```

