```

```mdl
test QA-6: Two people draw together
  desc: One person shares a diagram, a second joins from the link, and each sees the other's presence, cursor and shapes live.
  actors: human
  covers: [F-2.1, F-2.3, F-4.3, F-5.1, F-5.2, F-5.3, F-6.1, F-8.1, F-9.1, F-9.2]
  status: passing # 2026-11-15, chromium
  automated:
    - drawing-app:collaboration.spec.ts#Collaboration › two people draw together
  given:
    - two browser profiles, Ada and Ben, that have never opened the app, both online
  steps:
    - name: Ada draws
      do: As Ada, open the app, choose the Rectangle tool and drag out a rectangle.
      expect: the pill reads "My diagrams / Untitled" and the Views panel lists one rectangle
    - name: Ada shares
      do: As Ada, click Share, create a multi-use invitation and copy its link.
      expect: the dialog lists Ada as a member and one invitation; the link carries `?spaceInvitationCode=`
    - name: Ben joins
      do: As Ben, open the copied link.
      expect: Ben sees the join dialog, then Ada's diagram at the same `/<space id>/<diagram id>` path, with her rectangle, and Ben's space menu lists only "My diagrams"
    - name: Presence
      do: Leave both on the diagram for up to a minute.
      expect: each shows the other's avatar beside Share
    - name: Cursors
      do: As Ben, move the pointer over the canvas.
      expect: Ada sees a cursor with Ben's name follow it
    - name: Ben draws
      do: As Ben, choose the Ellipse tool and drag out an ellipse.
      expect: within a few seconds Ada's Views panel lists the rectangle and the ellipse
    - name: Ada adds a diagram
      do: As Ada, open the diagram menu, type "Roadmap" and choose New diagram “Roadmap”.
      expect: Ada's pill reads "Roadmap", and Ben's diagram menu lists "Roadmap" beside "Untitled"
```

```mdl
test QA-7: Follow a collaborator
  desc: Two people on one space; one follows the other from the presence list, across a zoom, a pan and a switch of diagram, until Stop ends it.
  actors: human
  covers: [F-9.1, F-9.3, F-9.4]
  status: passing # 2026-11-15, chromium
  automated:
    - drawing-app:collaboration.spec.ts#Collaboration › follow a collaborator
  given:
    - two browser profiles, Ada and Ben, that have never opened the app, both online
  steps:
    - name: Ada and Ben share a space
      do: As Ada, draw a rectangle and share; as Ben, open the link. As Ada, add a diagram "Roadmap" and draw a rectangle on it.
      expect: each shows the other's avatar beside Share; Ada is on "Roadmap" and Ben on "Untitled"
    - name: Ben follows Ada
      do: As Ben, click Ada's avatar beside Share and click Follow on her row.
      expect: Ada's row carries Stop in place of Follow until Ben's canvas opens her diagram and the list closes; Ben's canvas shows "Roadmap" at Ada's path, and both pills take the follow's amber wash and underline
    - name: Ada moves
      do: As Ada, zoom in with Ctrl and the wheel, then scroll the canvas.
      expect: within a second Ben's view shows Ada's rectangle at the same place and size as hers
    - name: Ada switches diagram
      do: As Ada, choose "Untitled" in the diagram menu.
      expect: Ben's canvas switches to "Untitled" at Ada's path
    - name: Ben stops
      do: As Ben, click Ada's avatar and click Stop on her row.
      expect: neither pill shows the follow's wash; Ada zooming and scrolling again leaves Ben's view where it is
```

```mdl
test QA-8: Across this app and Composer
  desc: A Composer user and a drawing.sh user share a space, draw on one diagram together, and follow each other between the two apps.
  actors: human
  covers: [F-5.2, F-9.1, F-9.2, F-9.3, F-9.5]
