## Changelog

```mdl
decision D-1: The app is a full-screen canvas editor, a canvas-editor counterpart of tldraw.com, open for anyone to use. It is an app-framework app built from plugins: its own layout plugin plus the canvas plugin.
  date: 2026-11-14
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-1]
```

```mdl
decision D-2: The identity is created automatically and is anonymous. Setting a display name and resetting the identity come later and are out of the initial scope.
  date: 2026-11-14
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-2]
```

```mdl
decision D-3: The app has a very simple space switcher, and diagrams live within a space.
  date: 2026-11-14
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-3, F-4]
```

```mdl
decision D-4: Users can send and receive invitations, kept simple by using delegated, non-interactive invitations.
  date: 2026-11-14
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-5, F-6]
```

```mdl
decision D-5: The app is compatible with Composer: someone invited to a space by a Composer user can collaborate on its diagrams and sees every diagram in the space.
  date: 2026-11-14
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-3.5, F-4, F-6.4]
```

```mdl
decision D-6: The app's UI uses only existing react-ui components.
  date: 2026-11-14
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-1.4]
```

```mdl
decision D-7: The name is decided later; drawing.sh, the existing site, is the fallback.
  date: 2026-11-14
  by: user:wittjosiah
```

```mdl
decision D-8: The plugin set is Attention, Client, Graph, ProcessManager, Theme, Illustrator, Canvas and `DiagramAppPlugin`, which contributes the layout, the React root and the root-collection rule. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-11-14
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-1.2, F-1.3]
  why: The canvas article needs attention, the graph its shortcuts resolve against, and the illustrator's variants; drawing.sh runs on the same set. Filing into the root collection is one capability, so the app contributes it rather than loading SpacePlugin.
  rejected:
    - SpacePlugin: brings Composer's navigator, deck surfaces and space settings, which a single-canvas app neither shows nor needs.
```

```mdl
decision D-9: A diagram is an illustrator `Drawing`. The app creates the 2D Canvas variant, lists drawings of every variant, opens the variants it registers, and shows a Composer notice for the rest. New drawings file into the root collection. Fills in [D-5].
  date: 2026-11-14
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-4.1, F-4.2, F-4.3, F-4.4]
  why: Composer's canvas diagrams are `Drawing`s with a `Canvas`; listing all variants keeps "see every diagram" true without shipping Excalidraw and tldraw.
  rejected:
    - Listing only Canvas drawings: hides diagrams Composer users made, against D-5.
    - Converting other variants on open: changes a Composer user's drawing just by looking at it.
```

```mdl
decision D-10: The invitation is Composer's share link: delegated, multi-use, known-public-key auth, carried in `?spaceInvitationCode=`. Fills in [D-4] and [D-5].
  date: 2026-11-14
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-5.1, F-5.2, F-6.1, F-6.4]
  why: The same link then opens in either app. EDGE redeems only NONE and KNOWN_PUBLIC_KEY invitations; with KNOWN_PUBLIC_KEY the keypair in the link is the secret, not the invitation id.
  rejected:
    - SHARED_SECRET: needs the interactive code exchange D-4 rules out, and EDGE never redeems it.
    - NONE: anyone who learns the invitation id from the space's control feed can join.
```

```mdl
decision D-11: First run creates "My diagrams" with one empty diagram; any other empty space shows an empty state, and joining never creates a space. Fills in [D-2] and [D-3].
  date: 2026-11-14
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-2.1, F-2.3, F-4.6]
  why: The app opens straight onto a canvas, but opening a shared space must not write into it.
```

```mdl
decision D-12: The client runs with EDGE signaling and with EDGE replicators and agents off; account-less identities sync peer to peer while another member is online. Fills in [D-5].
  date: 2026-11-14
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-7]
  why: Since edge#1510 an identity with no Hub account gets only swarm and signal frames; replicator frames are dropped and the space-root route returns 403, which the client retries forever. Turning replication on waits for [Q-2].
  rejected:
    - Replicators on: no data moves and every space logs 403 retries.
```

```mdl
decision D-13: The last space and the last diagram per space are remembered in this browser's local storage; the URL carries only an invitation. Fills in [D-3].
  date: 2026-11-14
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-2.2, F-3.2]
```

```mdl
question Q-1: What is the app called, and on which domain?
  date: 2026-11-14
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  context: drawing.sh is the fallback (D-7) but already hosts the agent-diagram DSL site. whois on 2026-11-14 reported these .sh names unregistered; a registrar must confirm.
  options:
    - linework.sh: a plain word for drawn lines, no well-known product with the name.
    - dotline.sh: dots and lines, what a diagram is made of; also free on .is and .to.
    - canvy.sh: short and says canvas; also free on .is, .ink and .to.
    - drawing.sh: the fallback; the app moves to its root and the DSL site to a path or subdomain.
```

```mdl
question Q-2: How do account-less identities get EDGE replication, so a diagram syncs when nobody else is online?
  date: 2026-11-14
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-7.2]
  context: EDGE admits account-less identities for signaling only (edge#1510). A Composer link still works, because the space's agent redeems it, but afterwards the joiner syncs only with the Composer user's devices while one is online.
  options:
    - Agent-backed spaces: EDGE lets an unbound identity's replicator frames through for spaces that have an EDGE agent; the owning account pays for storage. Covers spaces shared from Composer, not spaces made here.
    - Lightweight accounts: Hub mints an account for an unbound identity on first use, with storage and rate caps. Covers everything, agents included, and needs an abuse budget.
    - Peer-to-peer only: keep today's behaviour and say so in the UI.
```

```mdl
decision D-14: The space and diagram pill sits at the top center and carries the sync indicator at its end. Fills in [D-3].
  date: 2026-11-14
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-3.1, F-7.3, DiagramRoot]
  why: The canvas article draws its own toolbars in every corner and along the bottom edge (breadcrumb, palette, zoom, edit and view toolbars, inspector); the top center is the only free edge.
  rejected:
    - Top-left, as in the mockups: covers the breadcrumb and the palette.
    - Bottom-left with the indicator bottom-right: covers the zoom and view toolbars.
```

```mdl
decision D-15: A join fails only on a cancelled, expired or timed-out invitation or an observable error; the ERROR state alone does not end it, and an already-joined error counts as success. Fills in [D-4] and [D-5].
  date: 2026-11-14
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-6.3]
  why: The guest runs EDGE and peer-to-peer redemption at once. EDGE refuses a space with no agent as retryable and sets ERROR, while a member online admits the joiner a moment later. Composer's join panel ignores the ERROR state the same way.
  rejected:
    - Fail on ERROR: every join of a space made in this app fell back to a new space even though the member admitted it.
```

```mdl
decision D-16: `DiagramAppPlugin` contributes the `Collection` schema and fires its own start event before the first write, which pulls in the client's schema registration. Fills in [D-9].
  date: 2026-11-14
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-1.3]
  why: The root collection is a typed object, and the client registers schemas on demand; the client plugin's `types` option is ignored when the host passes its own client.
```

```mdl
decision D-17: The domain does not need to be on .sh, but the name should ideally be about diagrams. linework.sh, dotline.sh and canvy.sh are rejected.
  date: 2026-11-14
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [Q-1]
```

```mdl
question Q-3: Which diagram domain does the app use?
  date: 2026-11-14
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  context: Follows [D-17]. On 2026-11-14 these had no RDAP record and no nameservers; single-word names on new TLDs are often premium-priced, so a registrar must confirm price and availability. Registered already include diagram.sh, .app, .io, .so, .page, .new, .studio, .ink, .to, .dev, .ai and .co, and diagrams.new, diagrams.sh and diagrams.io.
  options:
    - diagram.space: matches the app's spaces, where diagrams live and are shared.
    - diagram.wiki: says anyone with a link can edit.
    - diagram.club: an open, social place to draw together; diagrams.club is also free.
    - diagram.is: short; reads as the start of a sentence.
    - diagramtogether.com: the only free .com found; long but says what the app does.
```

