```mdl
decision D-151: Export embeds the drawing, its `Canvas` and every model, layout and scene object the canvas references, with plugin-canvas's SVG export as the picture. Import keeps a `Canvas` drawing as it is and converts any other drawing, such as a drawing.sh render, to the `Canvas` variant in place. Fills in [D-145].
  date: 2026-11-19
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-11.1, F-11.3]
  why: A `.dx.svg` payload is a list of objects, and import gives them all fresh ids and rewrites the references between them, so a canvas and what it references travel whole. Shapes drawn by hand carry no DSL identity, so reading the scene as DSL would drop them.
  rejected:
    - Replaying the scene into a laid-out SVG drawing with its DSL source: only DSL-managed shapes come through, so a hand-drawn diagram exports empty.
    - Keeping an imported SVG drawing as it is: the app neither lists nor opens it ([F-4.4]).
```

```mdl
decision D-152: A link import lands in the space the app opens anyway, and a first run with an import fills "My diagrams" with the imported diagram in place of the empty one. A share's link is built on the environment's app origin, whichever host it was posted to. Fills in [D-145] and [D-146].
  date: 2026-11-19
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-11.5, F-12.1]
  why: A `?src=` or `?d=` link names no space. An empty "Untitled" beside the imported diagram is a diagram nobody asked for. The landing page posts to its own host, but the link it opens must name the app.
```

