decision D-166: The DXOS section has three pages: drawing.sh and DXOS (identity, spaces and the peer-to-peer note), Composer, and The DX CLI. The CLI page tells readers to install `@dxos/cli@next`, since `dx drawing` is not in the `latest` release, and to keep the app open while `dx` joins or imports, since the app syncs only with members online at the same time. It documents `dx drawing render`, `list`, `export` and `import`, `dx space join` with an app link, and `dx mcp serve`. Fills in [D-165].
